<article class="env-lemma" id="079W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/079W">Lemma <span data-tag="079W">20.28.1</span>.</a> Let $f : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. The functor $Rf_*$ defined above and the functor $Lf^*$ defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/06YJ" data-tag="06YJ">20.27.1</a> are adjoint: </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{O}_ X)}(Lf^*\mathcal{G}^\bullet , \mathcal{F}^\bullet ) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{O}_ Y)}(\mathcal{G}^\bullet , Rf_*\mathcal{F}^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> bifunctorially in $\mathcal{F}^\bullet \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (D(\mathcal{O}_ X))$ and $\mathcal{G}^\bullet \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (D(\mathcal{O}_ Y))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows formally from the fact that $Rf_*$ and $Lf^*$ exist, see Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/09T5" data-tag="09T5">13.30.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>